🚽 platform.brainrot — the input/time/window seam, raylib backing.
🚽
🚽 Every `plat_*` function takes the frame number even when it doesn't need
🚽 it, so that test/platform_fake.brainrot can implement the identical
🚽 signatures with a scripted input tape. That parity is what lets the
🚽 headless harness run the real simulation loop unchanged.
🚽
🚽 Requires `#cooked <raylib>` earlier in the including file.

🚽 Audio device BEFORE the window, and the order is not arbitrary.
🚽
🚽 With rl_init_audio_device() after rl_init_window(), this game aborts inside
🚽 PulseAudio -- `pa_mainloop_prepare: Assertion 'm->state == STATE_PASSIVE'`
🚽 -- reproducibly, 3 runs out of 3, on WSLg. Initialising audio first is
🚽 clean 5 runs out of 5 at 700 frames.
🚽
🚽 Worth recording what it is NOT, because all of these were checked: not the
🚽 rendering (it still aborted with drawing removed entirely), not the update
🚽 frequency (35,000 pumps in a standalone program are fine), not
🚽 rl_set_music_volume, not rl_is_audio_device_ready, and not the game's frame
🚽 rate, which is a steady 60. A standalone program making the identical audio
🚽 calls never reproduced it. The variable that mattered was starting
🚽 PulseAudio's client threads before GLFW's rather than after.
🚽
🚽 The ALSA backend does not care either way -- forcing it with
🚽 PULSE_SERVER=/nonexistent was clean before this change -- so this is a
🚽 PulseAudio-side race, not raylib misuse. Ordering it this way costs
🚽 nothing and avoids it.
skibidi plat_open() {
    rl_init_audio_device();
    rl_init_window(t_screen_w(), t_screen_h(), "TUNG TUNG TUNG SAHUR: RUN");
    rl_set_target_fps(60);
}

skibidi plat_close() {
    rl_close_window();
}

🚽 --- music ---------------------------------------------------------------
🚽
🚽 Behind the platform seam like everything else with a device behind it, so
🚽 the headless harness can no-op the whole thing.
🚽
🚽 Returns a handle, or -1 if there is no audio device or the file is
🚽 missing. -1 is not an error: the game runs silent. Someone cloning this
🚽 without the track, or running it over SSH, should still get a game.
rizz plat_music_open(rant path) {
    🚽 The device is already up -- see plat_open() for why it has to be.
    cap ready = rl_is_audio_device_ready();
    edgy (!ready) { bussin 0 - 1; }
    rizz m = rl_load_music(path);
    edgy (m < 0) { bussin 0 - 1; }
    rl_set_music_looping(m, W);
    rl_set_music_volume(m, t_music_volume());
    rl_play_music(m);
    bussin m;
}

🚽 Refills the decode buffer. This MUST be called every frame: raylib says
🚽 nothing if it is not, the track plays for a fraction of a second and
🚽 stops, and it looks exactly like a broken file.
skibidi plat_music_tick(rizz music) {
    edgy (music >= 0) { rl_update_music(music); }
}

🚽 --- sound effects -------------------------------------------------------
🚽
🚽 One-shots, so rl_load_sound rather than rl_load_music: decoded whole at
🚽 load and played without a per-frame pump. The distinction matters --
🚽 loading these as streams would mean remembering to update four of them
🚽 every frame, and loading the 82-second track this way would be tens of
🚽 megabytes of PCM.
🚽
🚽 Every one returns -1 when there is no audio device or the file is
🚽 missing, and plat_sfx_play() ignores that, so a missing effect is silent
🚽 rather than fatal.
🚽
rizz plat_sfx_ready() {
    cap ready = rl_is_audio_device_ready();
    edgy (ready) { bussin 1; }
    bussin 0;
}

🚽 ONE loader, taking the path. There were five of these, identical but for
🚽 a string literal, because a user-defined function could not take a
🚽 `rant`. Landed upstream with brainrot#311 -- see draw_load() for the
🚽 same story on the texture side.
rizz plat_sfx_load(rant path) {
    edgy (plat_sfx_ready() == 0) { bussin 0 - 1; }
    rizz s = rl_load_sound(path);
    edgy (s >= 0) { rl_set_sound_volume(s, t_sfx_volume()); }
    bussin s;
}

skibidi plat_sfx_play(rizz snd) {
    edgy (snd >= 0) { rl_play_sound(snd); }
}

skibidi plat_sfx_close(rizz snd) {
    edgy (snd >= 0) { rl_unload_sound(snd); }
}

skibidi plat_music_close(rizz music) {
    edgy (music >= 0) { rl_unload_music(music); }
    rl_close_audio_device();
}

chad plat_dt(rizz frame) {
    bussin rl_get_frame_time();
}

cap plat_jump_down(rizz frame) {
    cap a = rl_is_key_down(t_key_space());
    edgy (a) { bussin W; }
    cap b = rl_is_key_down(t_key_up());
    bussin b;
}

cap plat_bat_pressed(rizz frame) {
    cap a = rl_is_key_pressed(t_key_x());
    edgy (a) { bussin W; }
    cap b = rl_is_key_pressed(t_key_z());
    bussin b;
}

cap plat_start_pressed(rizz frame) {
    bussin rl_is_key_pressed(t_key_space());
}

cap plat_restart_pressed(rizz frame) {
    cap a = rl_is_key_pressed(t_key_r());
    edgy (a) { bussin W; }
    cap b = rl_is_key_pressed(t_key_space());
    bussin b;
}

cap plat_should_close(rizz frame) {
    bussin rl_window_should_close();
}

🚽 A state sample, called once per frame. Nothing in the real game wants
🚽 it, so here it does nothing; the headless harness prints it on a fixed
🚽 cadence to give the golden file something to catch drift with. Keeping
🚽 the seam in the shipping path is what stops the harness from needing
🚽 its own copy of the frame loop.
skibidi plat_trace(rizz frame, rizz score, rizz lvl, rizz hearts,
                   rizz combo, chad speed, chad py, chad dist) {
    rizz noop = 0;
}
